#180 (Intermediate 2) — [PA 2013 / Luogu P4694 / UVa 1660] Raper & Archive Companion [Luogu P4597 / CERC 2016] Sequence Maintenance

Canonical Slot: Ch 23 — Intermediate 2 (Int-2) | Wave Provenance: 4B-P10 & W6-12
Judge URLs:

Primary (Collinear-Slope WQS Regret Benchmark): https://www.luogu.com.cn/problem/P4694
Archive Companion (Online Streaming Slope Trick): https://www.luogu.com.cn/problem/P4597



Constraints & Problem Statements

Luogu P4694 [PA 2013] Raper: Over \(N \le 5 \times 10^5\) days, day \(i\) can record 1 CD in studio A (cost \(a_i\)) and master 1 CD in studio B (cost \(b_i\)), requiring \(i \le j\) for every matched pair \((i, j)\). Produce exactly \(K\) CDs at minimum cost. Unlike CF 802O, the test suite of PA 2013 Raper heavily stresses many duplicate values \(a_i, b_j\) (flat segments of \(C(k)\) where dozens of pairs have identical marginal cost \(\Delta_k = \lambda^*\)).
Luogu P4597: Streaming non-decreasing sequence maintenance (\(N \le 5 \times 10^5\)), answering the minimum \(\ell_1\) cost after insertions.



4-Step Compilation & Collinear Slope Analysis (P4694)

Step 1 (Diagnostic Signal): Mathematically identical to CF 802O, except P4694 is famous for breaking buggy WQS implementations that fail when \(C(k)\) has a long collinear plateau of slope \(\lambda^*\) around \(k = K\).
Step 2 (Why Naively Mixing &lt; 0 and &lt;= 0 Breaks): Suppose at \(\lambda = \lambda^*\), the minimum value of \(C(k) - k \lambda^*\) is achieved for all \(k \in [k_{\min}(\lambda^*),\; k_{\max}(\lambda^*)]\), where \(k_{\min}(\lambda^*) &lt; K &lt; k_{\max}(\lambda^*)\). If your inner heap comparator does not break ties on key using dcnt, then check(lambda) might return an arbitrary \(k\) inside \([k_{\min}, k_{\max}]\) that isn’t even monotone in \(\lambda\)!
Step 3 (Exact Monotone Tie-Breaking Contract): By ordering (key, dcnt) lexicographically (key ascending, then dcnt ascending so dcnt = 0 beats dcnt = 1 on equal keys) and only matching when pq.top().key + b[i] - lambda &lt; 0, check(lambda).second is guaranteed to equal \(k_{\min}(\lambda)\), which is a strictly monotone step function of \(\lambda\). Then best_lam is the largest integer \(\lambda\) such that \(k_{\min}(\lambda) \le K\), so \(K \in [k_{\min}(\text{best\_lam}),\; k_{\max}(\text{best\_lam})]\), and pen_cost + K * best_lam recovers the exact integer value \(C(K)\)!
Step 4 (Failure-Mode Guard): Ensure the binary search upper bound hi covers \(\max_i a_i + \max_j b_j \le 2 \times 10^9 + 5\).







Note3-Tier Progressive Hints (#180)






Hint 1: What happens in WQS binary search when \(k\) consecutive augmentations have the exact same marginal cost \(\lambda^*\)?
Hint 2: If a fresh prep token (a_i, dcnt=1) and a regret token (-(b_{j0} - lambda), dcnt=0) have the exact same key in the min-heap, which one should be popped first so cnt equals \(k_{\min}(\lambda)\)?
Hint 3: Pop dcnt = 0 first when using &lt; 0 (or dcnt = 1 first when using &lt;= 0), so all zero-marginal-gain swaps happen before new pairs are added!










TipComplete C++ Solution (Luogu P4694 — [PA 2013] Raper)





// Luogu P4694 — [PA 2013] Raper (Collinear-Safe WQS + Regret Min-Heap)
// Time: O(N log N log(max_A + max_B)), Space: O(N)
#include &lt;bits/stdc++.h&gt;
using namespace std;

struct Token {
    long long key;
    int dcnt; // 1 = new pair, 0 = regret replacement
    bool operator&gt;(const Token& o) const {
        if (key != o.key) return key &gt; o.key;
        return dcnt &lt; o.dcnt; // With &lt;= 0 condition, prefer dcnt = 1 to compute k_max(lambda)
    }
};

int main() {
    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);
