#181 (Advanced 1) — [UOJ #455 / LOJ #3043 / WC2019] 雪灾与外卖 & Archive Companion [CF 1251E2] Voting (Hard Version)

Canonical Slot: Ch 23 — Advanced 1 (Adv-1) | Wave Provenance: 4B-P14 / W6-07 & W6-13
Judge URLs:

Primary (1D Capacitated Line Transport with Batched Regret Heaps): https://uoj.ac/problem/455
Archive Companion (Backward Suffix Threshold Sweep): https://codeforces.com/problemset/problem/1251/E2



Constraints & Problem Statements

UOJ #455 [WC2019] 雪灾与外卖: On a 1D number line, there are \(N \le 10^5\) deliverymen at coordinates \(x_1 \le \dots \le x_N\) and \(M \le 10^5\) restaurants at coordinates \(y_1 \le \dots \le y_M\). Restaurant \(j\) has unit meal cost \(w_j\) and capacity \(c_j \le 10^9\) (\(\sum c_j \ge N\)). Assigning deliveryman \(i\) to restaurant \(j\) costs \(|x_i - y_j| + w_j\). Match all \(N\) deliverymen at minimum total cost.
CF 1251E2 Voting (Hard Version): \(N \le 2 \times 10^5\) voters; voter \(i\) joins for free if at least \(m_i\) voters have already joined, or can be bribed for cost \(p_i\). Minimize total bribe cost to win all \(N\) voters.



4-Step Compilation (UOJ #455 & CF 1251E2)

Step 1 (Non-Graph Diagnostic Signal): In UOJ #455, \(N, M \le 10^5\) and restaurant capacities \(c_j \le 10^9\) rule out unit-by-unit MCMF. Because a 1D line is a degenerate tree where \(\operatorname{dep}(u) = \text{coord}(u)\) and every left-to-right pair \((p \le q)\) has LCA \(p\) with distance \(q - p = (+q) + (-p)\), we can sweep coordinates left-to-right maintaining two run-length-compressed regret heaps Heap_X (deliverymen) and Heap_Y (restaurants)!
Step 2 (Two-Heap Telescoping Equations on a 1D Line):

Deliveryman arrives at \(x\): Must be matched immediately (equivalently, carries \(-\infty\) mandatory penalty). Pop the best available restaurant token (v, cnt) from Heap_Y. Pay \(x + v\). Now, what if a later restaurant \(y' \ge x\) wants to steal this deliveryman? The cost should change from \(x + v\) to \((y' - x) + \dots\), wait: no! What if a later deliveryman \(x' \ge x\) steals this restaurant \(v\) while \(x\) gets matched to a later restaurant \(y'\)? Using our Tree LCA Regret Formula (Theorem 23.2) at current coordinate \(l = x\) (where the new deliveryman has depth \(a = x\) and matched with restaurant token \(b = v\) from the left):

The cost paid is \(x + v\).
The new deliveryman regret token pushed into Heap_X has key: \[
a_{\text{reg}} = -(x + v) - x = -2x - v!
\] Let’s check: if a later restaurant at \(y' \ge x\) (weight \(w'\)) steals this deliveryman by matching with \(a_{\text{reg}}\), it adds \((y' + w') + (-2x - v) = (y' - x + w') - (x + v)\), which cancels the old restaurant match \(x + v\) and replaces it with the new match \(y' - x + w'\)!

Restaurant arrives at \((y, w, c)\):

First, push (w - y, c) into Heap_Y (representing up to \(c\) unused capacity slots for future deliverymen \(x' \ge y\)).
Next, while Heap_X has deliveryman tokens \(u\) such that \(u + y + w &lt; 0\) (and the restaurant still has remaining capacity from \(c\)): pop (u, cnt) from Heap_X, match \(k = \min(c_{\text{rem}}, \text{cnt})\) units for cost \(k \cdot (u + y + w)\), push the restaurant regret token (-2y - w - u, k) into Heap_Y (so a future deliveryman \(x' \ge y\) can steal this restaurant slot for \((x') + (-2y - w - u) + (u + y + w) = x' - y + w\)!), and accumulate total matched count \(K_{\text{matched}}\)!
Finally, coalesce all \(K_{\text{matched}}\) deliverymen that just switched to restaurant \(y\) into a single batched deliveryman regret token (-y - w, K_matched) in Heap_X!


Step 3 (Amortized Complexity Proof): Why is UOJ #455 \(O((N + M) \log(N + M))\) despite \(c_j \le 10^9\)? Because each deliveryman \(x_i\) has multiplicity \(1\) (pushing \(1\) node to Heap_X), and each restaurant \(y_j\) coalesces all \(K_{\text{matched}}\) deliverymen it steals into at most \(1\) new batched node in Heap_X, while pushing \(1\) restaurant regret node into Heap_Y per popped Heap_X node!
Step 4 (CF 1251E2 Suffix Sweep): In CF 1251E2, sorting voters by threshold \(m_i\) and sweeping \(k = N-1\) down to \(0\) guarantees that the suffix \(\{i : m_i \ge k\}\) must contain at least \(\max(0, k - \text{cnt}(m &lt; k))\) bribed voters. Pushing \(p_i\) for \(m_i = k\) into a min-heap and popping the cheapest until bribed &gt;= k - cnt_below[k] solves the problem in \(O(N \log N)\) without even needing regret tokens!







Note3-Tier Progressive Hints (#181)






Hint 1 (UOJ #455): When a deliveryman at \(x\) matches with a restaurant token of key \(v\) to his left (paying \(x + v\)), what regret key should be pushed into Heap_X so that a future restaurant at \(y' \ge x\) with meal cost \(w'\) can steal him for net total cost \((y' - x) + w'\)?
Hint 2 (UOJ #455): Answer to Hint 1: push -2*x - v into Heap_X, because (x + v) + (y' + w' - 2*x - v) = y' - x + w'! And when restaurant \((y, w, c)\) steals \(K\) total deliverymen from Heap_X, push a single batched token (-y - w, K) into Heap_X!
Hint 3 (CF 1251E2): Sweep threshold \(k\) backward from \(N-1\) down to \(0\), adding voters with \(m_i = k\) to a min-heap of bribe costs \(p_i\), and pop whenever cnt_below[k] + bribed &lt; k.










TipComplete C++ Solutions (UOJ #455 雪灾与外卖 & CF 1251E2)





// Solution 1: UOJ #455 — [WC2019] 雪灾与外卖 (Batched 2-Heap Simulated MCMF)
// Time: O((N + M) log(N + M)), Space: O(N + M)
#include &lt;bits/stdc++.h&gt;
using namespace std;

const long long INF = 1e14;

struct Node {
    long long key;
    long long cnt;
    bool operator&gt;(const Node& o) const { return key &gt; o.key; }
};

int main() {
    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);
    cin.tie(nullptr);
    int n, m;
    if (!(cin &gt;&gt; n &gt;&gt; m)) return 0;
    vector&lt;long long&gt; x(n);
    for (int i = 0; i &lt; n; ++i) cin &gt;&gt; x[i];
    struct Rest { long long y, w, c; };
    vector&lt;Rest&gt; r(m);
    long long sum_c = 0;
    for (int j = 0; j &lt; m; ++j) {
        cin &gt;&gt; r[j].y &gt;&gt; r[j].w &gt;&gt; r[j].c;
        sum_c += r[j].c;
    }
    if (sum_c &lt; n) {
        cout &lt;&lt; -1 &lt;&lt; "\n";
        return 0;
    }

    priority_queue&lt;Node, vector&lt;Node&gt;, greater&lt;Node&gt;&gt; pqX, pqY;
    // Sentinel infinite-cost restaurant at -INF so every deliveryman matches immediately
    pqY.push({INF, n});

    long long ans = 0;
    int i = 0, j = 0;

    auto process_deliveryman = [&](long long pos) {
        auto top = pqY.top();
        pqY.pop();
        ans += pos + top.key;
        if (top.cnt &gt; 1) pqY.push({top.key, top.cnt - 1});
        // Push regret token into pqX so a later restaurant can steal this deliveryman
        pqX.push({-2 * pos - top.key, 1});
    };

    auto process_restaurant = [&](long long pos, long long w, long long cap) {
        long long total_stolen = 0;
        while (!pqX.empty() && cap &gt; 0) {
            auto top = pqX.top();
            if (top.key + pos + w &gt;= 0) break;
            pqX.pop();
            long long take = min(cap, top.cnt);
            ans += take * (top.key + pos + w);
            cap -= take;
            total_stolen += take;
            if (top.cnt &gt; take) pqX.push({top.key, top.cnt - take});
            // Push restaurant regret token into pqY so a later deliveryman can reclaim top.key
            pqY.push({-2 * pos - w - top.key, take});
        }
        if (total_stolen &gt; 0) {
            // Coalesce all stolen deliverymen into ONE batched regret token in pqX!
            pqX.push({-pos - w, total_stolen});
        }
        if (cap &gt; 0) {
            pqY.push({w - pos, cap});
        }
    };

    while (i &lt; n || j &lt; m) {
        if (i &lt; n && (j == m || x[i] &lt;= r[j].y)) {
            process_deliveryman(x[i++]);
        } else {
            process_restaurant(r[j].y, r[j].w, r[j].c);
            j++;
        }
    }
    cout &lt;&lt; ans &lt;&lt; "\n";
    return 0;
}
// Solution 2: CF 1251E2 — Voting (Hard Version) (Backward Threshold Sweep + Min-Heap)
// Time: O(N log N), Space: O(N)
#include &lt;bits/stdc++.h&gt;
using namespace std;

void solve() {
    int n;
    cin &gt;&gt; n;
    vector&lt;vector&lt;long long&gt;&gt; buckets(n);
    for (int i = 0; i &lt; n; ++i) {
        int m;
        long long p;
        cin &gt;&gt; m &gt;&gt; p;
        buckets[m].push_back(p);
    }
    priority_queue&lt;long long, vector&lt;long long&gt;, greater&lt;long long&gt;&gt; pq;
    long long total_cost = 0;
    int bribed = 0;
    int rem_below = n;
    for (int k = n - 1; k &gt;= 0; --k) {
        rem_below -= (int)buckets[k].size();
        for (long long p : buckets[k]) pq.push(p);
        while (rem_below + bribed &lt; k) {
            total_cost += pq.top();
            pq.pop();
            bribed++;
        }
    }
    cout &lt;&lt; total_cost &lt;&lt; "\n";
}

int main() {
    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);
    cin.tie(nullptr);
    int t;
    if (cin &gt;&gt; t) while (t--) solve();
    return 0;
}







#182 (Advanced 2) — [ICPC WF 2018 / Luogu P6943] Conquer the World & Archive Companion [CF 1534G] A New Beginning

Canonical Slot: Ch 23 — Advanced 2 (Adv-2) | Wave Provenance: 4B-P15 / W6-15 & W6-14
Judge URLs:

Primary (Tree Mergeable-Heap Simulated Flow): https://qoj.ac/problem/2143 (also https://www.luogu.com.cn/problem/P6943)
Archive Companion (2D Diagonal Projection + Lazy-Shift Slope Trick): https://codeforces.com/problemset/problem/1534/G



Constraints & Problem Statements

[ICPC WF 2018] Conquer the World: Given an edge-weighted tree of \(N \le 2.5 \times 10^5\) vertices, vertex \(u\) starts with \(x_u\) armies and needs at least \(y_u\) armies (\(\sum x_u \ge \sum y_u\), \(\sum y_u \le 10^6\)). Minimize total movement distance to satisfy all demands.
CF 1534G A New Beginning: \(N \le 8 \times 10^5\) potatoes at \((x_i, y_i)\) (\(x_i, y_i \ge 0\)). Starting at \((0, 0)\) and moving only Right \((+1, 0)\) or Up \((0, +1)\), you can collect potato \(i\) from any point \((x, y)\) on your path by paying \(|x - x_i| + |y - y_i|\). Minimize total cost.



4-Step Compilation (Conquer the World & CF 1534G)

For Conquer the World: As proved in Theorem 23.2 (Section 23.3 Part B), at each vertex \(l\) (with weighted root depth \(d(l)\)), we merge children’s Leftist Heaps \(H_X(l)\) (supply keys) and \(H_Y(l)\) (demand keys, initialized to \(d(v) - M_{\infty}\) with \(M_{\infty} = 10^{12}\)). While \(\min(H_X(l)) + \min(H_Y(l)) - 2 d(l) &lt; 0\), we match \(k = \min(\text{cnt}_a, \text{cnt}_b)\) units and push both complementary regret keys: \[
a_{\text{reg}} = 2 d(l) - b \in H_X(l), \qquad b_{\text{reg}} = 2 d(l) - a \in H_Y(l).
\] At the end, add \((\sum_{v=1}^N y_v) \cdot M_{\infty}\) back to the answer!
For CF 1534G (Chebyshev Diagonal Projection + Two-Heap Slope Trick): When you step Right \((+1, 0)\) or Up \((0, +1)\), the sum coordinate \(s = x + y\) increases by \(+1\), while the \(x\)-coordinate either increases by \(+1\) or stays unchanged (\(x_{\text{next}} \in [x, x+1]\)). Furthermore, if you are on diagonal \(s_i = x_i + y_i\) at point \((x, s_i - x)\), the \(\ell_1\) distance to \((x_i, y_i)\) is: \[
|x - x_i| + |(s_i - x) - (s_i - x_i)| = 2|x - x_i|!
\] (Since moving \(1\) unit in \(x\) along the diagonal changes both \(x\) and \(y\), we can work in unit cost \(|x - x_i|\) directly!). Sort points by \(s_i = x_i + y_i\) ascending. Advancing from \(s_{\text{prev}}\) to \(s_{\text{cur}}\) by \(\Delta s\) widens the flat minimum interval \([L_{\min}, R_{\min}]\) of the DP function on the right by \(+\Delta s\) (simply shift_R += delta_s on the right min-heap \(H_R\)!), and adding \(|x - x_i|\) inserts \(x_i\) into the two-heap Slope Trick structure (H_L max-heap for slopes \(&lt; 0\), H_R min-heap for slopes \(&gt; 0\))!







Note3-Tier Progressive Hints (#182)






Hint 1 (Conquer the World): Why do we subtract \(M_{\infty} = 10^{12}\) from every initial demand token at \(v\), and why can’t the two regret tokens \(2 d(l) - b\) and \(2 d(l) - a\) ever match with each other?
Hint 2 (Conquer the World): Use a simple array-backed Leftist Heap storing (key, cnt) so merging subtrees takes \(O(\log N)\) time without pointer allocation overhead.
Hint 3 (CF 1534G): Transform \((x_i, y_i) \mapsto (s_i = x_i + y_i,\; x_i)\), sort by \(s_i\), maintain max-heap \(H_L\) and shifted min-heap \(H_R\), and update ans += max({0LL, H_L.top() - x, x - (H_R.top() + shift_R)})!










TipComplete C++ Solutions (Conquer the World & CF 1534G)





// Solution 1: [ICPC WF 2018 / Luogu P6943] Conquer the World
// Mergeable Leftist Heaps + Dual Regret Tokens
// Time: O((N + sum_Y) log(N + sum_Y)), Space: O(N + sum_Y)
#include &lt;bits/stdc++.h&gt;
using namespace std;

const long long INF = 1e12;
const int MAX_NODES = 2500005;

struct LeftistPool {
    long long key[MAX_NODES], cnt[MAX_NODES];
    int lc[MAX_NODES], rc[MAX_NODES], dist[MAX_NODES];
    int tot = 0;

    int new_node(long long k, long long c) {
        int u = ++tot;
        key[u] = k; cnt[u] = c;
        lc[u] = rc[u] = dist[u] = 0;
        return u;
    }

    int merge(int x, int y) {
        if (!x || !y) return x | y;
        if (key[x] &gt; key[y]) swap(x, y);
        rc[x] = merge(rc[x], y);
        if (dist[lc[x]] &lt; dist[rc[x]]) swap(lc[x], rc[x]);
        dist[x] = dist[rc[x]] + 1;
        return x;
    }

    void pop(int& root) { root = merge(lc[root], rc[root]); }
} hp;

int n;
vector&lt;pair&lt;int, long long&gt;&gt; adj[250005];
long long x_sup[250005], y_dem[250005], dep[250005];
int rootX[250005], rootY[250005];
long long total_cost = 0;

void dfs(int u, int p) {
    if (x_sup[u] &gt; 0) rootX[u] = hp.merge(rootX[u], hp.new_node(dep[u], x_sup[u]));
    if (y_dem[u] &gt; 0) rootY[u] = hp.merge(rootY[u], hp.new_node(dep[u] - INF, y_dem[u]));

    for (auto [v, w] : adj[u]) {
        if (v == p) continue;
        dep[v] = dep[u] + w;
        dfs(v, u);
        rootX[u] = hp.merge(rootX[u], rootX[v]);
        rootY[u] = hp.merge(rootY[u], rootY[v]);
    }

    while (rootX[u] && rootY[u]) {
        long long a = hp.key[rootX[u]];
        long long b = hp.key[rootY[u]];
        if (a + b - 2 * dep[u] &gt;= 0) break;

        long long ca = hp.cnt[rootX[u]];
        long long cb = hp.cnt[rootY[u]];
        long long k = min(ca, cb);

        total_cost += k * (a + b - 2 * dep[u]);

        if (ca == k) hp.pop(rootX[u]);
        else hp.cnt[rootX[u]] -= k;

        if (cb == k) hp.pop(rootY[u]);
        else hp.cnt[rootY[u]] -= k;

        // Dual-Heap Regret Rule (Theorem 23.2): push both complementary regret keys!
        rootX[u] = hp.merge(rootX[u], hp.new_node(2 * dep[u] - b, k));
        rootY[u] = hp.merge(rootY[u], hp.new_node(2 * dep[u] - a, k));
    }
}

int main() {
    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);
    cin.tie(nullptr);
    if (!(cin &gt;&gt; n)) return 0;
    for (int i = 1; i &lt; n; ++i) {
        int u, v;
        long long w;
        cin &gt;&gt; u &gt;&gt; v &gt;&gt; w;
        adj[u].push_back({v, w});
        adj[v].push_back({u, w});
    }
    long long sum_y = 0;
    for (int i = 1; i &lt;= n; ++i) {
        cin &gt;&gt; x_sup[i] &gt;&gt; y_dem[i];
        long long common = min(x_sup[i], y_dem[i]);
        x_sup[i] -= common;
        y_dem[i] -= common;
        sum_y += y_dem[i];
    }
    dfs(1, 0);
    cout &lt;&lt; total_cost + sum_y * INF &lt;&lt; "\n";
    return 0;
}
